WEBVTT

00:00.587 --> 00:02.226
- [Voiceover] Let F be
a function such that

00:02.226 --> 00:03.842
F of negative one is three.

00:03.842 --> 00:07.054
And F prime of negative
one is equal to five.

00:07.054 --> 00:08.770
Let G be the function G of X

00:08.770 --> 00:10.191
is equal to one over X.

00:10.191 --> 00:12.831
Let capital F be a function defined as

00:12.831 --> 00:15.438
the product of those other two functions.

00:15.438 --> 00:19.066
What is capital F prime of negative one?

00:19.066 --> 00:21.030
Well, we can just apply
the product rule here,

00:21.030 --> 00:22.462
let me just rewrite let me just

00:22.462 --> 00:25.154
essentially state the product rule.

00:25.154 --> 00:27.365
Capital F prime of X

00:27.365 --> 00:29.619
is going to be equal to

00:29.619 --> 00:31.929
since capital F of X is the product

00:31.929 --> 00:32.834
of these two functions,

00:32.834 --> 00:34.744
when we apply the product
rule this is gonna be

00:34.744 --> 00:35.744
F prime of X

00:36.903 --> 00:37.903
times G of X

00:39.297 --> 00:40.130
plus plus

00:41.595 --> 00:43.166
F of X

00:43.166 --> 00:44.749
times G prime of X.

00:46.328 --> 00:47.882
And so if we want to evaluate this

00:47.882 --> 00:49.918
at F of negative one

00:49.918 --> 00:51.727
capital F prime

00:51.727 --> 00:53.950
at negative one is equal to

00:53.950 --> 00:56.193
F prime of negative one

00:56.193 --> 00:58.110
times G of negative one

00:59.297 --> 01:02.932
plus function F evaluated at negative one

01:02.932 --> 01:04.845
times the derivative of G

01:04.845 --> 01:06.912
evaluated at negative one.

01:06.912 --> 01:09.271
And let's see if we can
figure these things out.

01:09.271 --> 01:11.531
So do they tell us this anywhere?

01:11.531 --> 01:12.732
Can we figure this out?

01:12.732 --> 01:14.428
F prime of negative one.

01:14.428 --> 01:15.482
Well they tell us right over here

01:15.482 --> 01:16.667
F prime of negative one

01:16.667 --> 01:18.330
is equal to five.

01:18.330 --> 01:20.578
So this is equal to five.

01:20.578 --> 01:22.548
Now, let's actually stick with F.

01:22.548 --> 01:24.332
What is F of negative one?

01:24.332 --> 01:25.868
Well, they tell that to us

01:25.868 --> 01:26.701
right over here.

01:26.701 --> 01:29.164
F of negative one is equal to three.

01:29.164 --> 01:32.083
So F of negative one is equal to three.

01:32.083 --> 01:33.612
Now G of negative one

01:33.612 --> 01:35.046
and G prime of negative one

01:35.046 --> 01:36.759
they don't give it to us explicitly here

01:36.759 --> 01:38.300
but we can figure it out.

01:38.300 --> 01:41.149
We can, we know that if G of X

01:41.149 --> 01:42.651
is equal to this

01:42.651 --> 01:45.026
G of negative one is equal

01:45.026 --> 01:46.696
to one over negative one

01:46.696 --> 01:48.697
which is equal to negative one.

01:48.697 --> 01:51.080
So this is equal to

01:51.080 --> 01:52.559
negative one.

01:52.559 --> 01:55.348
And then last but not least

01:55.348 --> 01:57.910
if we want to find G prime of negative one

01:57.910 --> 02:00.084
we just have to take
the derivative of this.

02:00.084 --> 02:01.417
So G prime of X.

02:02.598 --> 02:04.860
Actually just let me rewrite G of X.

02:04.860 --> 02:05.693
G of X

02:06.601 --> 02:08.164
one over X is just the same thing

02:08.164 --> 02:10.243
as X to the negative one.

02:10.243 --> 02:11.506
So we're gonna use a power rule

02:11.506 --> 02:13.246
to figure out G prime of X

02:13.246 --> 02:15.357
is equal to bring that exponent

02:15.357 --> 02:17.755
out front, negative one times X

02:17.755 --> 02:20.120
to the and then decrement the exponent

02:20.120 --> 02:22.307
negative two power.

02:22.307 --> 02:23.474
So, G prime of

02:24.891 --> 02:26.670
negative one

02:26.670 --> 02:28.735
of negative one is equal to

02:28.735 --> 02:30.235
negative one times

02:31.854 --> 02:33.437
negative one to the

02:34.275 --> 02:36.220
negative two power.

02:36.220 --> 02:38.375
And that's just the same thing as

02:38.375 --> 02:41.625
negative one over negative one squared.

02:43.423 --> 02:44.452
This is one.

02:44.452 --> 02:46.258
So this is just all going to evaluate

02:46.258 --> 02:47.591
to negative one.

02:49.388 --> 02:50.804
So this is

02:50.804 --> 02:52.123
negative one.

02:52.123 --> 02:53.869
And so we have

02:53.869 --> 02:55.491
five times negative one

02:55.491 --> 02:57.267
which is negative five.

02:57.267 --> 02:58.889
Plus three times negative one

02:58.889 --> 03:00.532
which is negative three.

03:00.532 --> 03:01.911
Which is equal to

03:01.911 --> 03:03.859
negative eight.

03:03.859 --> 03:05.755
So F prime of negative one

03:05.755 --> 03:08.005
is equal to negative eight.
